_:nc8826532fde24107aa142ec3863b50d6xb0	http://schema.org/description	"The year is 1613, and Shakespeare is acknowledged as the greatest writer of the age. But disaster strikes when his renowned Globe Theatre burns to the ground. Devastated, Shakespeare returns to Stratford, where he must face a troubled past and a neglected family. Haunted by the death of his only son, Hammlet, he struggles to mend the broken relationship with his wife and daughters. In so doing, he is ruthlessly forced to examine his own failings as a husband and father. This film is directed and starred by the outstanding drama actor and director Sir Kenneth Branagh."
