_:n74a1acd761e641e4b997ce229cac3471xb0	http://schema.org/description	"Based on the play by Noël Coward, &#39;Blithe Spirit&#39; tells the story of Charles Condomine (Dan Stevens, &#39;Downton Abbey&#39;), a widowed crime novelist who is ailed by writer&#39;s block as he attempts to complete his first screenplay. His second wife, Ruth (Isla Fisher &#39;Arrested Development&#39;), encourages him to keep it up, desperately wishing to relocate to Hollywood. In the search for inspiration, he and Ruth take part in a séance led by the eccentric Madame Arcati (Judi Dench, &#39;Skyfall&#39;) and accidentally summon Charles&#39; first wife, Elvira Condomine (Leslie Mann, &#39;Motherless Brooklyn&#39;). The jealous Elvira decides to stick around and haunt the couple. Except this supernatural love triangle has a sinister edge: Elvira wants to kill Charles, and even death won&#39;t stop her from doing it. &#39;Blithe Spirit&#39; is directed by Edward Hall (&#39;The Durrells&#39;) in his feature-film directorial debut. Piers Ashworth (&#39;Fisherman&#39;s Friends&#39;), Meg Leonard (&#39;Finding Your Feet&#39;) and Nick Moorcroft (&#39;Burke & Hare&#39;) adapt Coward&#39;s play for the screen. Joining the star-studded cast are Emilia Fox (&#39;Silent Witness&#39;), Julian Rhind-Tutt (&#39;Stardust&#39;), Aimee-Ffion Edwards (&#39;Peaky Blinders&#39;), James Fleet (&#39;Unforgotten&#39;) and Simon Kunz (&#39;Traitors&#39;). &#39;Blithe Spirit&#39; is set for a May 2020 release in the UK."
