_:naa84a786ce5c451aa77530c83598fa3axb0	http://schema.org/description	"Directed and written by Andrew Dominik, &#39;Blonde&#39; is a daring reinterpretation of the life of one of Hollywood&#39;s great legends: Marilyn Monroe. The filmmaker&#39;s rewritten story is based on the bestseller by Joyce Carol Oates, a five-time Pulitzer Prize-winning author. This feature film tells us about the unstable childhood of the most famous sex symbol on the planet, her life before becoming the iconic Marilyn, that is, her experiences as Norma Jeane Mortenson, her meteoric and impressive rise to fame, her love affairs, and a long etc. &#39;Blonde&#39; moves between fact and fiction to explore the widening gulf between Monroe&#39;s private and public life. It is a portrait that drinks from fiction to show us the experiences of the most famous actress of the 50s and 60s, a journey through a modern look at the culture of celebrities. As for the main cast, Ana de Armas gives life to Marilyn Monroe, along with Adrien Brody, who plays Arthur Miller, Bobby Cannavale as Joe Dimaggio and Sara Paxton is Miss Flynn. In addition, Julianne Nicholson, Xavier Samuel, Evan Williams, Lily Fisher, Caspar Phillipson and David Warshofsky, among others, complete the cast. &#39;Blonde&#39; premieres on Wednesday, September 27 in Spain, through the Netflix platform, in charge of distributing the film that will not reach the big screen and will only be available via streaming."
