_:necaefaae87b7469a81ee862367b4e9ecxb0	http://schema.org/description	"A scientist talks to the daughter of a serial killer, who is in a persistent vegetative state, so that she can get inside her mother?s mind for a test of extraordinary experimental technology. But the rehearsal does not go as expected and the young woman ends up waking up to the terrifying demons of the past, literally speaking. &#39;Demonic&#39; is directed and scripted by Neill Blomkamp. The film stars Carly Pope, Chris William Martin, Michael Rogers, Andrea Agur, Nathalie Boltt, Terry Chen. Media outlets like Austin Chronicle have praised this film: &quot;&#39;Demonic&#39; is Blomkamp at his most constrained since &#39;District 9&#39;, and it&#39;s a film with an intimacy that he&#39;s never risked before. He keys into a forgotten aspect of the holy text of possession films (...) where the opening hour is as much about the fallibility of medical science in the face of the supernatural as it is about Catholic angst. That&#39;s why it&#39;s his best feature since he unleashed hapless interstellar bugs on Johannesburg, while still serving up a radical change in tempo and direction. With a miniscule 10-person cast, and a smattering of well-placed VFX work, Demonic feels like someone crowbarred a V8 into a VW Beetle and handed the keys to a champion racer. &#39;Demonic&#39; rips open new technical possibilities for horror&quot;."
