_:n61cba2c687cb411ea2477c8100b85eeexb0	http://schema.org/description	"The famous architect Gusave Eiffel has finished his collaboration in the construction of the Statue of Liberty. Just when he seems to be at the top of his career, the French government is trying to convince him to design a spectacular building to be the symbol of the Universal Exhibition that will take place in Paris in 1889. However, Eiffel does not seem to have any interest in the project. Just when it looks like nothing?s going to change his mind, a mysterious woman he knew comes back to his life. The resurgence of this forbidden love inspires the architect to build what will be his masterpiece, changing the skyline of the French capital forever, and becoming part of History. This is the story of how the Eiffel Tower was made and also of its builder and the steps he followed to create it. With Emma Mackey (&quot;Sex Education&quot;) and Romain Duris (&quot;All the money in the world&quot;), under the direction of Martin Bourboulon (&quot;Daddy or Mommy&quot;), this story, will show the depths of the construction of the Eiffel Tower."
