_:n68bf3e4cfde64223b252a2c250807b5bxb0	http://schema.org/description	"&#39;Les gardiennes de la planète&#39; is a documentary directed and signed by Jean-Albert Lievre (&#39;Le syndrome du Titanic&#39;) that explores and shows the life of whales. Inspired by Heathcote Williams&#39; bestseller, &#39;Whale Nation&#39;, this feature film shows us the life of these great creatures and discovers some territories that are still unexplored alike the little known society that is that of the whales. From the struggle between life and death when one of them is stranded on the shore of a remote beach, to their long-distance journeys across the ocean, seeing their extraordinary abilities and their extremely rich and complex lives. A film that aims to show the diversity of species that exists on our planet and raise awareness about the place of the human being on it, showing the need for cooperation that we have all the species that inhabit the Earth. Jean Dujardin (&#39;The Wolf of Wall Street&#39;) is the narrator of this story accompanying the images recorded by Richard Sidey. Producted by Julien Seul and Marc Dujardin in collaboration with Michel Merkt, Géraldine Ohana and Olivier Wargny, who work as coproducers. In the sound department, crucial to get the spectacular sound emitted by whales, is Maxime Champesme in the recording and Alexandre Hernanez as editor."
