_:n401e491f1bac4e7a9b017531015537fcxb0	http://schema.org/description	"&#39;Motherless Brooklyn&#39; takes us to the New York of the fifties, where Lionel Essrog (Edward Norton), a withdrawn private detective who suffers from Tourettes syndrome (a syndrome characterised by the manifestation of multiple tics, both physical and vocal), will have to resolve one of the most importante murders of his professional career: that of his mentor and only friend Frank Minna (Bruce Willis). Armed only with a few clues and his obsessive mentality, this detective manages to unravel the best kept secrets about the fate of New York. Passing through gin-soaked jazz clubs in Harlem, the slums of Brooklyn and, finally, the golden halls of the powerful businesses in New York, Lionel fights the most dangerous and corrupt man in the city with all that he&#39;s got to honor his friend and save the woman who might be his own salvation. The film is stars, and is also written and directed by, Edward Norton (&#39;Birdman&#39;, &#39;American History X&#39; and &#39;Primal Fear&#39;). Joining the cast are Bruce Willis (&#39;Die Hard&#39;, &#39;Pulp Fiction&#39;), Willem Dafoe (&#39;Spider-Man&#39;, &#39;The Florida Project&#39;), Leslie Mann (&#39;Knocked Up&#39;, &#39;The Other Woman&#39;), Alec Baldwin (&#39;The Departed&#39;, &#39;It&#39;s Complicated&#39;) and Gugu Mbatha-Raw (&#39;The Beauty and the Beast&#39;), Bobby Cannavale (&#39;The Irishman&#39;, &#39;Jumanji&#39;), Cherry Jones and Michael Kenneth Williams."
