_:n41be3b7c286446acbf5b3010ace97b69xb0	http://schema.org/description	"The film portrays five days in the anti-terrorist service of the French police after the jihadist attacks in the Bataclan theater. &#39;November&#39; delves into the heart of the French anti-terrorist service, which fights against time to find the keys and the guilty people of a massacre that collapsed not only a city, but an entire country. A work that reveals all the research processes in a situation of uncertainty and incomprehension, but also of pain and mourning. &#39;November&#39; is the second highest-grossing French film of 2022 in France and received nominations for best director, best actor, best supporting actress (for two different performers), best editing and best sound at the 48th César Awards. The main cast of &#39;November&#39; is composed by Jean Dujardin, Anaïs Demoustier, Sandrine Kiberlain, Jérémie Rénier, Lyna Khoudri, Marine Vacth, Cédric Kahn, Sami Outalbali, Stéphane Bak, Sofian Khammes, Annabelle Lengronne and Sedina Balde. &#39;November&#39; is a film directed by Cédric Jimenez, director of &#39;Who&#39;s the Boss: Boss of Scandalz Strategyz&#39;, &#39;The Man with the Iron Heart&#39; and &#39;The Connection&#39;, among other titles. Olivier Demangel, writer of &#39;Atlantique&#39; and &#39;9-Month Stretch&#39;, among other titles, writes the script of the film."
