_:ned5ff26e8905466682abf328b3365c06xb0	http://schema.org/description	"&#39;A Day at Disney&#39; is a collaboration between Disney Publishing Worldwide and Disney +. The film, based on the book with which it shares the title, accompanies those men and women of enormous talent who have given life to some of the most popular Disney stories both in the audiovisual sector and in all the rest: theme parks, musicals ... This feature length documentary tells the fascinating and inspiring personal stories of 10 creatives responsible for the company&#39;s enduring magic. Through the perspective of Bob Iger, the former owner of the American giant, the film tells the daily lives of each one of them, offering us an intimate vision of their wonderful career, as well as their most important works. In short, this documentary exerts a panoramic vision of how the great ideas generated at Disney take shape until they reach the public. The magic of Disney from its beginnings to its maximum expression, delighting children and adults. And if this were not enough, the narrator of the documentary is the actor Sterling K. Brown, winner of two Emmy awards for &#39;The People v. O. J. Simpson: American Crime Story &#39;and&#39; This is us&#39;, and from the Golden Globe thanks to his role in the latter."
