_:n8d57836366d743939e1916e98e229707xb0	http://schema.org/description	"Amleth is a young Viking prince who is ready to become a grown man. Suddenly, his uncle Fjolnir kills his father, King Aurvandill, and kidnaps his mother, Queen Gudrún. The boy manages to escape and leaves the island in a boat while swearing he will take revenge for what happened. After 20 years, Amleth has become a fanatical berserker warrior or &#39;ulfhednar&#39; who lives raiding, robbing and looting Slavic villages. However, an old woman half witch half seer will remind him the vow he made two decades ago: to avenge his father and save his mother by murdering his uncle. With that goal clear in his mind, Amleth returns to Iceland on a slave ship and infiltrates his uncle&#39;s farm without being discovered, thanks to the help of the slave Olga. Written (with Sjón Sigurdsson) and directed by Robert Eggers, &#39;The North Man&#39; tells the story that inspired William Shakespeare&#39;s Hamlet. It has a stellar cast, including Alexander Skasgard (&#39;Melancholia&#39;, &#39;Godzilla vs. Kong) in the leading role; Nicole Kidman (&#39;Eyes Wide Shut&#39;, &#39;The Others&#39;) as the queen; Claes Bang (&#39;The Square&#39;), as the uncle; Ethan Hawk (&#39;Before Sunrise&#39;, &#39;Boyhood&#39;) as the king; Anya Taylor-Joy (&#39;Multiple&#39;, &#39;Last Night in Soho&#39;) who returns to work with the director after &#39;The Witch&#39;; Willem Dafoe (&#39;Spider-Man&#39;, &#39;Grand Budapest Hotel&#39;), who also returns to collaborate with Eggers after &#39;The lighthouse&#39; or Bjork, who returns to the cinema after her role in &#39;Dancer in the dark&#39;."
