_:n485ee655beee474996687505f60e92b4xb0	http://schema.org/description	"As summer approaches again, kids from different places come together to attend AdironACTS, a scrappy summer camp in upstate New York that&#39;s a haven for budding artists. After its indomitable founder, Joan, falls into a coma, her clueless son, &quot;crypto-bro&quot; Troy, is tasked with keeping this actor&#39;s paradise running. With financial ruin in the offing, Troy must join forces with Amos, Rebecca-Diane and their crew of eccentric professors to find a solution before the curtain rises on opening night. Joining forces for the first time, feature film directing duo Molly Gordon and Nick Lieberman celebrate the deranged, brilliant educators and magical spaces that allow children to be themselves and find their confidence, honing the details after decades of experimentation of life in a camp. With an award-winning cast and boundless creativity, &#39;Theater Camp&#39; carries potential cult followers squarely on its sequined shoulders, delivering us quotable lines and lovable, hilarious characters in a funny kind of comedy that deserves a round of applause. In the movie we can find Ben Platt as Anos, Molly Gordon as Rebecca-Diana and Amy Sedaris as Joan, the woman owner of the camp that falls in coma. The movie was presented in the past Sundance Film Festival."
