_:nfce5bfd5eecd4977a29a0c52efc244a0xb0	http://schema.org/description	"Based on the novel by Michael Crichton, the writer decided to direct and write the screenplay for the film adaptation. In the near future there is a huge amusement park is divided into three zones: the majestic Roman Empire, the Europe of the Middle Age and the distant and wild western from United States. Each of the areas is faithfully recreated and its actors are not people, but robots that reproduce reliably customs of the time. This park was created with the intention of attendees can live their own adventures at the time they choose it and, at the same time, learn in a fun and educational way. Peter Martin and John Blane are two friends who decide to go to the amusement park to spend a very pleasant time. Everything seems perfect, since robots are controlled by a central computer controlled latest technology. However, something goes wrong in the system, causing the failure behavior of robots and engaged in running violently. In the midst of this, a robot gunslinger pursue decide Peter and John tirelessly to capture them."
