_:n182f5e718736433d8781c9ebb4ce77bfxb0	http://schema.org/description	"The film &#39;Whitney&#39; is a deep, authentic and honest portrait of the artist and her family. What his documentary aesthetic aims to do is probe beyond sensationalist headlines and shed new light on the fascinating life trajectory of Houston. The well-known artist from New Jersey gained popularity for her fantastic voice and starred in several films before falling into a spiral of scandals to end her tragic death at 48 years of age. Thanks to the unpublished material from the archive: recordings, performances, audios and interviews with people from his immediate surroundings, director Kevin Macdonald dusts off the hidden scenes of Whitney&#39;s life, the voice that made millions of people fall in love. Years after her death, her voice, her songs and her personality continue to make her an unforgettable figure in the history of music and television."
